// #440, THE RUST-SHAPED CARRIER: an `FnOnce` closure held in a struct field
// whose type is a generic parameter bounded `F: FnOnce() -> String`. The first
// call moves the captured `String` out; the second frees it again. Measured as
// a LIVE DOUBLE FREE — compiled rc 0, linked, ran, `free(): double free
// detected in tcache 2`, exit 134. rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024 refuses the
// twin: error[E0382]: use of moved value: `h.f`.
//
// TWO FACTS WERE PRESENT AND NEITHER WAS ASKED FOR. The CONSUMING side already
// marked the path `h.f` moved. The READING side asked `moved_vars_` about the
// callee NAME, and the callee here is a PLACE — so the same call marked `h.f`
// moved twice and refused nothing. And `callable_is_fn_once` was a hand copy of
// `callable_call_mode` narrowed to a bit, stale exactly where it mattered: it
// read the family off `trait_name()`, which only a written `dyn FnOnce`
// carries, never off the family bits a LITERAL's type has carried since
// ADR 0029 S1. One call site moded the call `Once` while the other answered
// `false` about the same type.
//
// ⚠ ITS SIBLING CARRIER IS STILL OPEN AND NOT BY OVERSIGHT: with the field
// declared `f: || -> String` the type is the ERASED form, which states no
// Fn-family at all (ADR 0029 D5 — what a bare `|T| -> R` DECLARATION means is
// undecided, and reading it as `Fn` was implemented and refuted). That carrier
// is the queue row closure_field_fnonce_called_twice_double_free (#440).
package closure_field_fnonce_generic_called_twice;
use logos.mem.string;

struct H<F> where F: FnOnce() -> String { f: F }

fn main() -> i32 {
    let s: String = String::from("abcd");
    let h = H { f: move || -> String { return s; } };
    let a: String = (h.f)();
    let b: String = (h.f)();
    if a.len() != 4i64 { return 1i32; }
    if b.len() != 4i64 { return 2i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
// rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024: REFUSED — error[E0382]: use of moved value: `h.f`.
